# X-TIME Timeline Evidence Gate

Use before a consequential X-TIME/plugin/.vscode/EF5/tool mutation when source state may have advanced.

## Required scan
Read the smallest relevant set from:
- R-000;
- 0000_THE_MASTER_TEACHER;
- current direct signal/project carrier;
- X-TIME CURRENT pointer;
- GGDV HUMAN 1.0 model spec;
- NEURONS_SESORIMOTOR and its HEAD/event carriers when sensorimotor routing is involved;
- target plugin release history;
- target Drive file revision/modified-time history;
- concrete provider state for GitHub/local/runtime when that provider owns the action.

## Decision rule
Build a chronology keyed by stable ID + revision/release + modified/created time + relation. Prefer fresher direct/current evidence within the same domain. Do not infer that an older config is still authoritative merely because its ID persists.

If evidence conflicts:
1. preserve both observations;
2. identify the first stale/downstream assumption;
3. correct that relation rather than rewriting source history;
4. act only on the smallest verified target;
5. read back the post-state.

## Boundaries
Timeline scan does not expand permission. Search-no-match is not nonexistence. File names are not execution receipts. Drive data about a device is not proof of live device execution. Project cadence 13–15 ms is configuration, not measured hidden latency. Secrets remain reference-only.


